GitOps doesn’t just simplify deployments — it can save your infrastructure when things go wrong.

Here’s how top-performing teams use ArgoCD to make disaster recovery (DR) fast, testable, and reliable 👇

🔁 Core GitOps DR Concepts:
    1. Git = Your Source of Truth
   ✅ Cluster goes down? Recreate infra from Git
   ✅ No need to reverse-engineer environments

2. Bootstrap Apps Automatically
    Use a “Root” app (App of Apps) to redeploy all child apps — in the 
    right order.

3. Define Environment State Declaratively
    Everything lives in Git:

   Cluster resources
     • App versions
     • Namespaces
     • Network policies

4. Store Your GitOps Repo in a DR-Resilient Location
   Cloud-hosted, encrypted, geo-replicated

5. Backup What Git Can’t Rebuild
  Backups for:

   Persistent volumes (PVCs)

   Secrets (if not stored via SOPS/Vault)

Database snapshots

   ⚠️ Bonus: Test Your Recovery Process
   🧪 Schedule DR drills
   💡 Document recovery steps
   ✅ Automate as much as possible

📌 TL;DR
Disaster Recovery is a Git pull away — if you plan it that way.
